      "statement": "REFERENCE_FRAME_METHOD supplies principles and STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE one optional profile; neither selects, adopts or owns a Product binding. Existing Product authority owns its declaration and every grant. reference_frame_bases must be non-empty; each entry names the declaration URI, every admitting Goals/Product/requirement/accepted-design/other lawful authority and exact applicable Product/context/tenant/outcome/scope. The declaration owns the selected frames, method/profile, outcome, actor rules, envelopes, grants, triggers, coverage, results and invalidation; the JSON entry only locates it and its authority relation, neither contains the binding nor adopts/restates/authorizes frames. Method-cut inclusion makes a profile available; only Product authority adopts it; only exact authorized work instructions activate a bound frame for an actor and subject. Activation does not mutate the overlay, which neither registers agents, assigns permanent frames nor persists temporary configurations. Names or broad frames grant no semantic, operational, review, acceptance or disposition authority beyond cited owners and exact activation.",
