      "statement": "Minimum cases preserve: evaluation Frame versus consumer runtime Frame, with no nominal enrollment; specialist evaluation Owner versus semantic/decision owner, with no acquired owner authority; immutable released Product versus mutable Product Definition, selected only by occurrence context; build Tenant versus hosted/customer/account/runtime/data tenancy, with no build-tenancy default; and User roles/person/principal/account/actor/operator/data subject as unresolved until downstream authority defines or explicitly relates meanings. A positive local case declares one context and resolves exactly one concept; a positive cross-context case supplies the complete authorized relation. Negative cases include zero candidates, multiple candidates after disambiguation, selected concept outside candidates, context-free glossary fallback, incomplete coordinates, authority/basis mismatch, undeclared loss and invalidated relations. Guessed meaning cannot pass through correct downstream behavior.",
