      ],
      "key": "constitutional_surface_preservation",
      "statement": "A view cannot change a claim's meaning or authority under the selected constitution. Standards operate only as one complete released version admitted by release authority. Compressions, templates, comments, candidates, installed copies and mutable source cannot become partial constitutions or reinterpret owners. Derived instructions preserve applicability, obligations, permissions, exclusions, decision owners and invalidators; correct digests do not excuse losing a prohibition's condition or lawful alternative. Compression cannot strengthen or weaken relations; references must resolve within the actor's access or required meaning must be supplied directly. STDO owns normative construction algebra, authority, abstract state/transition laws, admissibility, necessary causal order and evidence invariants; consumers own concrete types, schemas, files, tools, runtimes, orchestration, tests and executable conformance. A shared-method amendment cannot itself create tools, workflow engines, runtimes, assurance systems or consumer realizations as STDO Product scope. Recording a ruling cannot widen its subject, implication, authority or change class. Mutable source may author future cuts but must not silently govern consumers.",
