      ],
      "key": "constitutional_chain_preservation",
      "statement": "Downstream success requires adequate upstream meaning and traceable authority; Goals/Product owners select outcomes and Design selects any allowed realization, not a uniquely derived implementation. Observations bind declared boundaries; events are durable carriers where selected. Projection is checked against source and current state, creates no second truth and need not require complete event replay. Repricing follows intake-selected class and owner: a constitutional gap changes that layer and affected downstream span without automatically requiring new Goals/Intent; unresolved causes can require more observation. Broken links, including no repricing path, unowned requirements, ungrounded design or realization lacking design decisions, create accidental law. Workspace state persists: each activation's current material state and valid authority define A; Z is admitted acceptance constraints. Actors acquire sufficient context for the next bounded transition; discarded context does not rewind A. Observation may invalidate beliefs/results but cannot silently change Z or grant permission; revising Z uses owning re-entry. GOALS.md carries the temporary work wave; PRODUCT.md states present-tense mutable Product definition, terms and boundaries, not immutable RC or installed Product. Requirements cover all constitutional obligations, not only features. Design chooses structural realization, topology, carriers, control/runtime wiring and lawful tenant boundaries. The what/how split is independent of layout.",
