      "key": "sprint_scope_escrow_close",
      "statement": "A sprint must not create, supersede, weaken or override Goals/Intent/Product/Requirements/Design authority. It states at least served goal/wave, upstream authority, admitted scope, excluded Product/requirement/design/runtime/data-contract/governance boundaries, expected change classes, any deferrable local proof/compliance debt, closure trigger/law and paydown/repricing path. Proof deferral is lawful only while local, visible, bounded and repayable. Escrow cannot satisfy method/release/Product closure until paid down, explicitly accepted under governing method, or repriced upstream. Close may be recommended—not automatically required—on timebox expiry, scope attainment, changed-area cost exceeding review, unsafe review uncertainty or gaps outgrowing the container. Close compares work/evidence with authority, classifies every gap, accepts compliant work, opens local-debt paydown and escalates drift lawfully. Discovery of any Product-truth change, including goal/intent/Product/requirement/design/runtime/data-contract/governance change, does not authorize landing it: split, escalate, reprice or explicitly carry paydown under governing method. Ticket Method owns mechanics; domain refinements may define appropriate escrow use.",
