      "key": "ambiguity_visibility_and_policy",
      "statement": "Unsupported meaning cannot become established result or permission. Graph/runtime F_D, F_P and F_H remain graph-native ODD concepts absent explicit import/translation. The chain progressively narrows priority, direction/scope, Product shape/terms, obligations, executable class, structure and implementation detail. Major ambiguity cannot hide in operator judgment, precedent or silent model choice. Each major boundary detects/records ambiguity, affected invariant/asset/decision boundary, decision if work proceeds, and resolved/carried/escalated/blocked handling. Declared Product policy and risk appetite determine lawful probabilistic carrying/decision versus explicit human adjudication, never convenience; lower risk appetite escalates more, higher permits more bounded probabilistic choice, but both record ambiguity and decision. The aim is visible governed progressive reduction to sufficient constraint, not elimination of all ambiguity before any work.",
