      "key": "ambiguity_results_and_hard_stops",
      "statement": "For 'identified ambiguity is resolved under governing meaning', established resolution is satisfied, established remaining ambiguity falsified, and insufficient evidence indeterminate, retaining invalid_basis/out_of_frame diagnoses. Carried/escalated ambiguity may remain unresolved. Separately, policy/authority-bound handling is satisfied when supported lawful, falsified on demonstrated violation, indeterminate when unsupported, with the same diagnoses; neither settles delivery or grants authority beyond policy. Hard stops apply regardless of risk appetite; typical classes are violated invariants/guarantees, absent required authority, missing declared execution/operation capability, undeclared irreversible effects and explicit human-approval gates. Witnessed violation or unmet required authorization falsifies the relevant admissibility predicate; missing evidence leaves it indeterminate. Fulfillment is separate: refusal proves neither failed outcome, non-performance nor absence of effects. Unusable basis and out-of-capability evaluation retain their diagnoses; undeclared or uncertain effects require actual observation before dependent action.",
