      "statement": "Product and requirements must supply enough constitutional signal for design to derive the lifecycle or explicitly record unresolved ambiguity. Product definition names material boundary, use context, release/install, live-use, observability and retirement/supersession postures. Requirements state governing invariants across build, assurance, release, deployment, usage, telemetry, retirement, ownership, source truth, authority and interpretation. Deferring a phase requires naming deferment and its later owning surface. Unknown phases require named gaps such as Gap: or Unanswered:; inapplicability requires why. This is ambiguity detection, not a requirement that every clause be a release plan. Missing lifecycle meaning cannot be supplied by convention, implementation precedent, prompts or fixtures: reprice its constitutional owner or carry explicit governed debt.",
