      ],
      "key": "intake_diagnosis_and_authority",
      "statement": "Bugs, features, issues, regressions, operator findings, release blockers and scenario failures use the same triage; none bypasses it for code/tests/release. Determine whether change is substantive, affected Product/scope, lawful class/re-entry, downstream surfaces/evidence to reprice/rederive/reprove, and release-scope fit or repricing. Diagnose current subject, outcome, observations and any predictive model, distinguishing defective realization, inadequate requirements/design, inaccurate prediction and insufficient observation; unresolved alternatives can select observation before repair. Severity is consequence and priority response order within mandate; neither changes diagnosis nor grants repair. A bug list is a view, not another route. Triangulation uses applicable frames over the same subject/basis, their material variables, relations and evidence, retaining alternatives/uncertainty and smallest sufficient repair scope. Exposing frame need not contain cause; relabeled repeated analysis adds no evidence. Intake binds selected outcome, interpreted meaning, current observations and actual owner; demonstrated implementation defects may support lower re-entry, while implementation-versus-requirement uncertainty stays unresolved. Bind exact report, governing sources, workspace/external observations, retained results and actual assessment grant; currentness controls reuse. Computed treatment decides candidate-versus-governing correction. Select the smallest sufficient applicable frame configuration, with localization where required, without prescribing reviewer count or another round; independence and repair authority remain.",
